Another command to know is the "N" or "#name" command.
"Nn" will name ("call") a *type* of objects, "Ny" will name ("name") an 
*individual* object.

So for instance after testing a whistle, you might "call" it "no
apparent effect" (using "Nn" or "#name[enter]n").  Then you can see if
other whistles you find are the same type of whistle.  Of course, in
some cases individual objects, rather than types, make the difference;
it depends.

